WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.528 --> 00:00:17.892
Kayla groaned as she joined Kobe and Jenny at a table.

2
00:00:19.713 --> 00:00:22.373
"I hate science experiments."

3
00:00:22.393 --> 00:00:27.155
"Science experiments are fun," Jenny said.

4
00:00:27.175 --> 00:00:29.735
"We just need a good idea."

5
00:00:32.492 --> 00:00:33.253
Kayla sighed.

6
00:00:33.273 --> 00:00:36.696
"I'm sick of making volcanoes explode."

7
00:00:36.716 --> 00:00:41.480
"We could grow mold," Kobe said.

8
00:00:42.521 --> 00:00:43.382
Jenny made a face.

9
00:00:44.463 --> 00:00:45.724
"Mold is gross."

10
00:00:47.585 --> 00:00:48.506
Kayla looked bored.

11
00:00:50.088 --> 00:00:51.929
She ripped a sheet of paper from her notebook.

12
00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:53.691
Jenny frowned.

13
00:00:55.112 --> 00:00:58.034
"Mr. Netter said we're supposed to work together, Kayla.

14
00:00:58.315 --> 00:00:59.396
You're not helping us."

15
00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.802
Kayla was folding wings on a paper airplane.

16
00:01:07.203 --> 00:01:08.844
"Let's test this plane."

17
00:01:08.864 --> 00:01:10.765
"Huh?" Kobe said.

18
00:01:10.785 --> 00:01:14.787
"We can measure how far it flies," Kayla said.

19
00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:17.068
"Good idea!"

20
00:01:17.489 --> 00:01:18.089
Kobe said.

21
00:01:18.109 --> 00:01:22.872
"It sounds scientific and fun," Jenny agreed.

22
00:01:24.052 --> 00:01:25.113
She looked at her notebook.

23
00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:30.176
"Step one of the scientific method is to ask questions."

24
00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:35.499
"How about, how does weight affect flight distance?"

25
00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:36.519
Kobe said.

26
00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:38.321
Everyone nodded.

27
00:01:39.202 --> 00:01:40.382
Jenny wrote down the question.

28
00:01:42.424 --> 00:01:45.026
"Next we have to come up with a hypothesis.

29
00:01:46.207 --> 00:01:48.249
That's a guess about what will happen."

30
00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.612
The kids did some research about airplane flight.

31
00:01:52.632 --> 00:01:56.515
"Hmm," said Kayla.

32
00:01:57.236 --> 00:01:59.698
"I think a lighter plane will fly farther."

33
00:01:59.718 --> 00:02:02.160
"Me too," Kobe said.

34
00:02:03.144 --> 00:02:07.207
"That's our hypothesis: a light paper plane will fly farther."

35
00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.308
Jenny wrote it down.

36
00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:16.453
"To test our hypothesis, we'll have to change the plane's weight."

37
00:02:19.075 --> 00:02:20.336
Kobe got some paperclips.

38
00:02:22.017 --> 00:02:23.578
"We can use these to add weight."

39
00:02:24.999 --> 00:02:26.240
Kayla grabbed her airplane.

40
00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.641
"Let's find a runway!"

41
00:02:30.503 --> 00:02:32.164
The kids went out into the hallway.

42
00:02:35.416 --> 00:02:39.659
Kayla threw the plane and Kobe measured where it stopped.

43
00:02:39.679 --> 00:02:40.400
"My turn!"

44
00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.321
said Kobe.

45
00:02:41.341 --> 00:02:46.544
"We should try to throw the plane the same way each time," said Jenny.

46
00:02:46.564 --> 00:02:49.867
"So Kayla should keep flying the plane."

47
00:02:52.889 --> 00:02:57.293
Kayla flew the plane several more times and Kobe measured each flight's distance.

48
00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:01.676
Next they added two paperclips to the plane.

49
00:03:04.256 --> 00:03:06.317
They flew and measured several more times.

50
00:03:07.737 --> 00:03:09.077
Jenny recorded the results.

51
00:03:12.138 --> 00:03:15.339
"Let's try four paperclips now," Kayla said.

52
00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.300
They flew the plane again.

53
00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:21.521
"Time to analyze our data!"

54
00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:22.381
Kobe said.

55
00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:26.503
"Uh-oh." Jenny studied the results with a frown.

56
00:03:26.523 --> 00:03:32.104
"Our plane flew farthest with two paperclips.

57
00:03:32.124 --> 00:03:34.066
Our hypothesis was incorrect."

58
00:03:34.086 --> 00:03:36.669
"That's okay," Kobe said.

59
00:03:36.689 --> 00:03:40.773
"Mr. Netter said a science experiment is for testing ideas.

60
00:03:42.295 --> 00:03:45.778
Even if your hypothesis is incorrect, you still learn stuff."

61
00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:47.941
Kayla grinned.

62
00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:53.226
"I learned something—science experiments can be fun!"
